Actually i was going through [this](https://dev.to/open-wc/generating-typescript-definition-files-from-javascript-5bp2) article, according to it, with newer version of typescript compiler it is possible to compile a .js file with jsDoc annotations and generate type definitions.
I checked it with `max` function of `d3-array` and it worked.

max.js with jsDoc annotations
```
/**
 * @function
 * @template T
 * @param {Iterable<T>} values 
 * @param {(value:T, index: number, values:Iterable<T>) => any } [valueof] 
 * @returns {T}
 */
export default function max(values, valueof) {
  let max;
  if (valueof === undefined) {
    for (const value of values) {
      if (value != null
          && (max < value || (max === undefined && value >= value))) {
        max = value;
      }
    }
  } else {
    let index = -1;
    for (let value of values) {
      if ((value = valueof(value, ++index, values)) != null
          && (max < value || (max === undefined && value >= value))) {
        max = value;
      }
    }
  }
  return max;
}
```
command I run
```
tsc max.js --allowJS --declaration --outDir ./out
```
Generated max.d.ts
```
/**
 * @function
 * @template T
 * @param {Iterable<T>} values
 * @param {(value:T, index: number, values:Iterable<T>) => any } [valueof]
 * @returns {T}
 */
export default function max<T>(values: any, valueof?: (value: T, index: number, values: any) => any): T;
```

However, I am not sure it would work for every case (does not worked for jsDoc `@yields` annotation ), but I think it can speed up the process.

